name tank-jettison-1
timeout 32000

# THE THIRD RUN OF THE RANGE TRIPLE — tank-radius-tanks.fbm with the two empty tanks LET GO. Two lines
# differ from that file: `brief_master_arm arm` and two `brief_release_s`.
#
# WHERE THE TWO TIMES COME FROM: measured, not chosen. In tank-radius-tanks.fbm the total fuel reaches
# 6,972.0 lb — the model's own INTERNAL capacity, to the digit — at t = 7,285.8 s, which is the moment
# JSBSim has emptied both external tanks and has not yet touched an internal one. That number is itself
# the proof of the draw order: FlightBox wrote one integer per tank (`propulsion/tank[i]/priority`) and
# `FGPropulsion::ConsumeFuel` did the rest. The jettison is briefed just after it.
#
# WHAT THE DIFFERENCE MEASURES, and it is the whole point of a tank being a tank: an empty tank is not
# free. Letting it go takes 240 lb of dry mass AND 0.475 ft^2 of drag area off each station, in the same
# call that empties and DESELECTS its fuel tank, so a run flown against tank-radius-tanks.fbm shows what
# an empty tank costs while it still hangs there.
#
# READING RULE: exit 2 (fuel exhaustion at cruise altitude, then the ground) is the correct outcome, as
# in both other files of the triple. The measurement is the distance at flameout against
# tank-radius-tanks.fbm's, plus the two `TANK_JETTISON` lines in `events.log`, each of which reports the
# fuel that went with the tank (here 0 lb: they were dry, which is what the anchor describes).
#
# THE SIMPLIFICATION, stated because it is one: a tank leaves through the ONE release path every store
# leaves by, so this mission has to arm the master switch to drop a fuel tank. The real jet's selective
# jettison is a separate control and does not (doc/modules/stores.md §Gaps).

unit viper
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn 46.90000 6.00000 8000 90.0 400       # 8,000 m ASL, due east, 400 KCAS
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100                       # 6,972 lb internal ...
  set store 4 tank370                        # ... plus 2,276 lb in the left wing tank
  set store 6 tank370                        # ... plus 2,276 lb in the right wing tank
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode off
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set brief_release_s 7300                   # both tanks measured dry at t = 7,285.8 s
  set brief_release_s 7305
  wp 46.90000 75.00000 8000 400              # ~5,200 km: further than any fuel state here reaches
